@startuml
title Wallet-authenticated SSH: preserved flow with planned browser integration
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox

actor User
participant "OpenSSH + PAM\n(implemented)" as SSH
participant "solana-authd\n(implemented)" as AuthD
participant "Auth gateway\n(production planned)" as Gateway
participant "Browser + wallet\n(planned)" as Wallet
participant "Solana RPC" as RPC

group Start one connection-bound login
  User -> SSH : ssh ubuntu@<server>
  SSH -> AuthD : PAM IPC: start(version=1, unix_user)
  AuthD -> AuthD : Generate exact challenge; 5-minute lifetime
  AuthD -> Gateway : POST /v1/sessions (bearer token)
  Gateway --> AuthD : 201 Created
  AuthD --> SSH : challenge: URL + expires_at
  SSH --> User : Open signing URL; press Enter after signing
end

group Wallet message signature
  User -> Wallet : Open /v1/sessions/{id}
  Wallet -> Gateway : Fetch exact published challenge
  Gateway --> Wallet : challenge_base64 + session_id + expires_at
  Wallet -> Wallet : Decode bytes; display server/account;\nsign with Phantom / Solflare
  Wallet -> Gateway : POST response {wallet, signature_base64}
  Gateway --> Wallet : 202 Accepted (submission only)
  User -> SSH : Return to SSH and press Enter
  SSH -> AuthD : PAM IPC: wait(version=1)
  AuthD -> Gateway : GET response (bearer token)
  Gateway --> AuthD : Proof, or 204 while pending
end

group Daemon signature and authorization checks
  AuthD -> AuthD : Verify original bytes, signature,\nexpiry, and session binding
  AuthD -> RPC : Finalized getAccountInfo: discover owner
  RPC --> AuthD : Server + context slot
  AuthD -> RPC : Finalized getMultipleAccounts with minContextSlot\nServer, subscription, owner + wallet grants
  RPC --> AuthD : Combined snapshot + context slot
  AuthD -> RPC : getBlockTime for combined slot
  RPC --> AuthD : Block time
  AuthD -> AuthD : Validate ownership, PDAs, roles, bindings,\nenabled state, expiry, and freshness
end

alt All checks pass before expiry
  AuthD -> AuthD : Consume session once
  AuthD --> SSH : allow=true
  SSH --> User : PAM_SUCCESS; configured user's shell
else Invalid proof, timeout, disconnect, or service/access failure
  AuthD --> SSH : Deny when connection is available
  SSH --> User : Authentication denied
end
AuthD -> Gateway : Best-effort DELETE session (bearer token)

note over SSH, RPC
  Local tests use a CLI signer and synthetic gateway/RPC services.
  Only the daemon authorizes login. No transaction or SOL payment occurs during login.
  Grant changes and expiry affect new logins; existing SSH sessions remain open.
end note
@enduml
